# Decision logging (required)

Whenever a change affects this project's structure, architecture, conventions, or standards, append a brief one-line note to `docs/decisions.md`.

## Format

```
- YYYY-MM-DD — decision — one-line why.
```

Newest entries first at the top of the list.

## Rules

- Brief is fine — one line per decision, not an essay.
- Log the decision in the same change that introduces it. Do not leave it for later or batch it up.
- Before finalizing a change, read `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/content-authoring.md`, `docs/design-system.md` (incl. motion grammar + performance rules), `docs/navigation.md`, and `docs/backlog.md` and follow their patterns; if your change deviates from them, that deviation is exactly what must be logged.

## What to log

- New content-layer rules or changes to frontmatter contracts
- New dependencies, tooling, or build steps
- Renamed routes, sections, or collections (`content/`, `lib/content/`, etc.)
- Changed styling approach or design-token conventions
- Navigation, hierarchy, or content-correctness rule changes (docs/navigation.md)
- Color, selection, or background treatment changes (docs/design-system.md color identity)
- Motion/animation changes (docs/design-system.md motion grammar)
- Performance-affecting changes: entrance animations, font preloading, image loading, new above-fold resources (docs/design-system.md performance rules)
- Altered verification workflow (lint/build/test expectations)
- Any deliberate deviation from an existing documented pattern

## What NOT to log

- Routine content edits (adding/editing an MDX file, fixing copy or typos)
- Mechanical refactors with no architectural impact
- Bug fixes that don't change conventions

Also keep `AGENTS.md` in sync if a rule there becomes stale.
